"use strict";(self.webpackChunksmart_barcode_scan_and_ordering_doc=self.webpackChunksmart_barcode_scan_and_ordering_doc||[]).push([[900],{4155(e,t,r){r.r(t),r.d(t,{_pageData:()=>n,default:()=>s});var a=r(641);const n=JSON.parse('{"path":"/smart-barcode-scan/order-status.html","title":"Order Status","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Order Status","description":"The Picked, Packed and Shipped order statuses, the scan-to-advance fulfilment chain, the tracking-code prompt and the OTP confirmation."},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"smart-barcode-scan/order-status.md"}'),o={name:"order-status.md"},s=(0,r(6262).A)(o,[["render",function(e,t,r,n,o,s){const d=(0,a.g2)("RouteLink");return(0,a.uX)(),(0,a.CE)("div",null,[t[13]||(t[13]=(0,a.Fv)('<h1 id="order-status" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#order-status"><span>Order Status</span></a></h1><p>Smart Barcode Scan and Ordering adds three order statuses to WooCommerce and a way to move an order through them by scanning it. This gives a packing bench real checkpoints instead of one long jump from Processing to Completed.</p><h2 id="the-added-statuses" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#the-added-statuses"><span>The added statuses</span></a></h2><table><thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Picked</strong></td><td>The items have been collected from the shelves</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Packed</strong></td><td>The parcel has been packed and is ready to hand over</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Shipped</strong></td><td>The parcel has left the building; a tracking code is recorded</td></tr></tbody></table><p>They appear immediately after <strong>Processing</strong> everywhere WooCommerce lists order statuses — the status filters at the top of <strong>WooCommerce → Orders</strong>, the Status dropdown on the order edit screen, the bulk-actions menu, and WooCommerce reports.</p><p><img src="/smart-barcode-scan-and-ordering/images/smart-barcode-scan/smart-barcode-order-statuses.png" alt="Picked, Packed and Shipped in the WooCommerce order list"></p><h2 id="advancing-an-order-by-scanning-it" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#advancing-an-order-by-scanning-it"><span>Advancing an order by scanning it</span></a></h2><p>This is the fastest route and the one the extension is designed around.</p><ol><li>Scan the order label. The popup opens on the <strong>Orders</strong> tab with the order loaded.</li><li>Scan the <strong>same</strong> order label again.</li><li>The order moves one stage forward, a success message names the new status, and the popup refreshes with the updated order.</li></ol><p>Scan it again for the next stage. The chain is:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Current status</th><th>Next status after a scan</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pending payment · On hold</td><td>Processing</td></tr><tr><td>Processing</td><td>Picked</td></tr><tr><td>Picked</td><td>Packed</td></tr><tr><td>Packed</td><td>Shipped — <strong>a tracking code is required</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Shipped</td><td>Completed — <strong>a confirmation is required</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Completed</td><td>Stays Completed: <em>&quot;Order #<code>&lt;id&gt;</code> is already Completed.&quot;</em></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Any other status (Cancelled, Refunded, Failed, Draft) is left untouched and the console simply reports the current status.</p><p>Every advance writes an order note in WooCommerce — <em>&quot;Status updated via Barcode Scanner scan.&quot;</em> — and an entry in the scan history.</p><div class="hint-container note"><p class="hint-container-title">Note</p><p>The order must be open in the <strong>Orders</strong> tab for a re-scan to advance it. Scanning an order while you are on the Inventory or Create Order tab loads it instead.</p></div><h2 id="the-tracking-code-prompt" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#the-tracking-code-prompt"><span>The tracking-code prompt</span></a></h2><p>An order cannot become <strong>Shipped</strong> without a shipping/tracking code. When you advance a <strong>Packed</strong> order, or select <strong>Shipped</strong> in the Status dropdown, the console asks for one.</p><p><img src="/smart-barcode-scan-and-ordering/images/smart-barcode-scan/smart-barcode-shipping-code.png" alt="Enter Shipping Code prompt"></p><ol><li>Type the carrier&#39;s tracking code (for example <code>TRK123456789</code>).</li><li>Click <strong>Confirm</strong>.</li></ol><p>Leaving it empty shows <em>&quot;Shipping code is required.&quot;</em> and nothing changes. <strong>Cancel</strong> abandons the status change.</p><p>The code is stored on the order and is shown again the next time that order is scanned.</p><h2 id="the-otp-confirmation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#the-otp-confirmation"><span>The OTP confirmation</span></a></h2><p>Moving an order from <strong>Shipped</strong> to <strong>Completed</strong> normally means the customer has taken delivery and confirmed it. When you make that change yourself, the console asks you to confirm you are closing the order without that verification.</p><p><img src="/smart-barcode-scan-and-ordering/images/smart-barcode-scan/smart-barcode-status-transition.png" alt="Status Transition confirmation"></p><p>Click <strong>Yes</strong> to proceed, or <strong>Cancel</strong> to leave the order as Shipped.</p><p>The same confirmation appears in the standard WooCommerce order screens: changing an order&#39;s status from Shipped to Completed on the order edit page, or using the &quot;complete&quot; action in the orders list, prompts <em>&quot;Are you sure you want to change the status without OTP?&quot;</em> before it proceeds.</p><h2 id="setting-a-status-directly" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#setting-a-status-directly"><span>Setting a status directly</span></a></h2><p>You do not have to follow the chain. With an order open in the <strong>Orders</strong> tab:</p><ol><li>Click the <strong>Status</strong> dropdown in the order header.</li><li>Choose any WooCommerce status.</li><li>Click <strong>Save Order</strong>.</li></ol><p>The tracking-code prompt and the OTP confirmation still apply to the Packed → Shipped and Shipped → Completed transitions when you use the dropdown.</p><div class="hint-container important"><p class="hint-container-title">Important</p><p>Choosing a status in the dropdown does not save it on its own — you must click <strong>Save Order</strong>. Advancing by scanning, on the other hand, saves immediately.</p></div><h2 id="setting-the-status-when-creating-an-order" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#setting-the-status-when-creating-an-order"><span>Setting the status when creating an order</span></a></h2>',31)),(0,a.Lk)("p",null,[t[1]||(t[1]=(0,a.eW)("New orders built in the ",-1)),t[2]||(t[2]=(0,a.Lk)("strong",null,"Create Order",-1)),t[3]||(t[3]=(0,a.eW)(" tab carry whatever status you choose in the ",-1)),t[4]||(t[4]=(0,a.Lk)("strong",null,"Order Status",-1)),t[5]||(t[5]=(0,a.eW)(" section of its sidebar. The default is ",-1)),t[6]||(t[6]=(0,a.Lk)("strong",null,"Processing",-1)),t[7]||(t[7]=(0,a.eW)(". See ",-1)),(0,a.bF)(d,{to:"/smart-barcode-scan/create-order.html#step-6-choose-the-order-status"},{default:(0,a.k6)(()=>[...t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,a.eW)("Create Order",-1)])]),_:1}),t[8]||(t[8]=(0,a.eW)(".",-1))]),t[14]||(t[14]=(0,a.Fv)('<h2 id="changing-several-orders-at-once" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#changing-several-orders-at-once"><span>Changing several orders at once</span></a></h2><p>The three statuses are available as WooCommerce bulk actions:</p><ol><li>Go to <strong>WooCommerce → Orders</strong>.</li><li>Tick the orders you want.</li><li>Choose <strong>Change status to picked</strong>, <strong>Change status to packed</strong> or <strong>Change status to shipped</strong> from <strong>Bulk actions</strong>.</li><li>Click <strong>Apply</strong>.</li></ol><div class="hint-container warning"><p class="hint-container-title">Warning</p><p>The bulk actions are standard WooCommerce status changes. They do <strong>not</strong> ask for a tracking code, so orders bulk-moved to Shipped will have no code recorded. Use the scan flow, or the Status dropdown in the console, whenever the tracking code matters.</p></div><h2 id="next-step" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#next-step"><span>Next step</span></a></h2>',5)),(0,a.Lk)("ul",null,[(0,a.Lk)("li",null,[(0,a.bF)(d,{to:"/smart-barcode-scan/order-scanning.html"},{default:(0,a.k6)(()=>[...t[9]||(t[9]=[(0,a.eW)("Order Scanning",-1)])]),_:1}),t[10]||(t[10]=(0,a.eW)(" — the rest of the order screen.",-1))]),(0,a.Lk)("li",null,[(0,a.bF)(d,{to:"/smart-barcode-scan/scan-logs.html"},{default:(0,a.k6)(()=>[...t[11]||(t[11]=[(0,a.eW)("Scan Logs",-1)])]),_:1}),t[12]||(t[12]=(0,a.eW)(" — the record of every status change made through the console.",-1))])])])}]])}}]);